course: dictionary
lesson: 4719
title: Hoover: a word from a brand name
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words start as the name of a product. In Britain and Ireland, hoover began as the brand name of a vacuum cleaner, and now people use it as an ordinary word for cleaning a carpet. «Can you hoover your room?» means "Can you clean your room with a vacuum cleaner?"
explain: Check the words around it. In «He hoovered up his dinner», the word up and the word dinner are your clues. Hoover up here means to eat something very fast, not to clean. Ask: does the sentence talk about a floor, or about food? That tells you which meaning fits.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «She helps with the hoovering, and tells her teacher when Nana seems poorly.» Hoovering here means cleaning with a vacuum, because a helper does chores at home. If the sentence still makes sense with your meaning, you are probably right.
fact: Hoover can be a verb: hoover, hoovers, hoovered, hoovering.
fact: A Hoover, with a capital H, is the brand name, and a hoover with a small h can mean any vacuum cleaner in the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand.
fact: «Hoover» means to clean a floor or carpet with a vacuum cleaner.
fact: «Hoover up» means to eat or take something in very fast.
fact: English makes new verbs from nouns, like «to hoover» and «to google», so a brand name can become an everyday word.
exercise: «Can you hoover your room?» What does hoover mean here? | To eat very fast | To paint the walls | To sing loudly | *To clean the floor with a vacuum cleaner
exercise: Grandad says, «He hoovered up his dinner.» What does hoovered up mean? | Carefully tidied the table | Left it on the plate | *Ate it very fast | Cooked it slowly
exercise: Mum says, «Please get the hoover out.» What is the hoover? | A bucket for water | A type of bird | A bin for rubbish | *A vacuum cleaner
test: «Mum paid her for hoovering the stairs.» What does hoovering mean here? | Counting the stairs | Painting the stairs | *Cleaning the stairs with a vacuum cleaner | Climbing the stairs fast
test: Why does «Hoover» have a capital H when it means the brand? | It is a rude word | It is at the start of a sentence | *It is a name, so it starts with a capital letter | It is a country
exam: Yesterday, Sam ___ the carpet. | *Hoovered | Hoover | Hoovering | Hoovers
